WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.827
A missing connection is an added rule that lets the premises reach a proposed conclusion.

2
00:00:06.127 --> 00:00:08.772
It must supply what the argument actually lacks.

3
00:00:09.072 --> 00:00:10.928
Every woven mat is labelled.

4
00:00:11.228 --> 00:00:14.193
The author concludes that every woven mat is stored.

5
00:00:14.493 --> 00:00:15.965
Start with a woven mat.

6
00:00:16.265 --> 00:00:20.297
The premise gets us to labelled, but there is no rule from there to stored.

7
00:00:20.597 --> 00:00:23.861
Adding labelled → stored closes this argument.

8
00:00:24.161 --> 00:00:28.727
Stored → labelled does not: it points back from the desired result.

9
00:00:29.027 --> 00:00:37.965
Another sufficiently strong premise might also close the argument, so test the offered candidates rather than demand one memorized wording.

10
00:00:38.265 --> 00:00:42.767
This introduces missing-link reasoning before full assumption applications.

11
00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:48.400
The aim is to see the exact gap between the proved condition and the required result.

12
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.751
Keep the conclusion as a rule when it is conditional.

13
00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:56.061
Identify the result the premises reach from its sufficient condition.

14
00:00:56.361 --> 00:01:00.415
After selecting a missing connection, run the entire argument again.

15
00:01:00.715 --> 00:01:03.808
Do not stop at finding a familiar noun in the answer.

16
00:01:04.108 --> 00:01:09.953
Check direction, compound requirements and whether the proposed conclusion is now unavoidable.
